    "id": "p066",
    "name": "University of Cincinnati",
    "hasFellowship": true,
    "fellowshipName": "Gap year scholars program",
    "description": "The Cincinnati Neurosurgery Gap Year Scholars Program provides two medical students with a year of neurosurgery research, clinical exposure, structured mentorship, and career development between their third and fourth years. Scholars may conduct basic-science, clinical-outcomes, database, or quality-improvement research through Cincinnati Children’s and the University of Cincinnati. They also attend neurosurgical conferences, participate in clinical services, and may present their research at national meetings. Each scholar receives $50,000 to support tuition, living expenses, and conference travel.",
    "link": "https://www.cincinnatichildrens.org/education/clinical/student-grad/neurosurgery/contact",
    "requirements": "Applicants must be enrolled in an LCME-accredited MD program or COCA-accredited DO program without a home neurosurgery residency and have a declared interest in neurosurgery. Before the July 1 start date, applicants must complete their core M3/OMS3 rotations—including at least one month of general or subspecialty surgery—and pass USMLE Step 1 or COMLEX Level 2. Applications require a CV, board-score report, two recommendation letters, a commitment letter from the applicant’s medical school, a one-page personal statement, and a one-page research statement identifying interests and potential University of Cincinnati neurosurgery mentors. Applications are considered from October through January, with interviews in March",
    "requirementLink": "",
    "builtForNoHome": true
