    "name": "University of Washington",
    "hasFellowship": true,
    "fellowshipName": "NREF Program",
    "description": "The Neurosurgery Research & Education Foundation (NREF) Medical Student Summer Research Fellowship awards $2,500 to medical students for a summer research project focused on understanding, treating, or preventing neurological disorders or improving patient care, under the mentorship of an investigator who is a member of the American Association of Neurological Surgeons (AANS)",
    "link": "https://nref.org/research/medical-student-fellowships/",
    "requirements": "Applicants must be enrolled in an accredited MD or DO program in the United States, Canada, or Mexico and must have completed at least one year of medical school before the fellowship begins. Applicants need a neurosurgery-related research project, an AANS-member sponsor or co-mentor, a three-page NIH-style proposal, and three separate recommendation letters. PhD, MD/PhD, gap-year, and post-baccalaureate students are ineligible. The 2027 application deadline is November 8, 2026.",
